# Read `rules.md` First

Before starting **any** implementation task in this project (new feature, page,
API route, schema change, or edit to existing code), read `rules.md` at the
project root in full.

- `rules.md` contains the non-negotiable project rules (stack, styling,
  roles, ZATCA/printing constraints, error handling, etc.) for Hisabi POS.
- If a task's instructions seem to conflict with `rules.md`, flag the conflict
  to the user instead of silently picking one side.
- This applies every session, not just the first time — rules.md may be
  updated over time, so re-read it rather than relying on memory of a past
  read.
